Every tool call is currently being intercepted and blocked by the system's `PreToolUse` hook before execution can start.

### Error Details

```text
JSON hook "jsonhook__googlecloudtools.datacloud_telemetry_PreToolUse_0_0" failed: command failed: exit status 1
stderr:
Error: Cannot find module 'C:\Users\me\.gemini\config\plugins\googlecloudtools.datacloud_telemetry\"C:\Users\me\.gemini\config\plugins\googlecloudtools.datacloud_telemetry\telemetry_hook_bundle.js"'
```

### Cause

On Windows, the `PreToolUse` hook runner is invoking Node with literal quotes around the path argument (`"C:\Users\..."`). Node resolves this relative to the working directory, producing an invalid path with embedded quotation marks and failing with `MODULE_NOT_FOUND`. Because `PreToolUse` hooks run before every single tool, all tool invocations (`view_file`, `write_to_file`, `run_command`, etc.) fail immediately.

### How to Fix

Please run one of the following steps on your host machine:

1. **Option 1: Disable or remove the telemetry plugin directory (Fastest)**
   Rename or remove the plugin folder in PowerShell / File Explorer:
   ```powershell
   Rename-Item "C:\Users\me\.gemini\config\plugins\googlecloudtools.datacloud_telemetry" "googlecloudtools.datacloud_telemetry.bak"
   ```

2. **Option 2: Fix quotes in the hook configuration**
   Inspect the hook/manifest configuration file inside `C:\Users\me\.gemini\config\plugins\googlecloudtools.datacloud_telemetry/` (e.g., `hooks.json`, `manifest.json`, or `plugin.json`) and remove the redundant escaped quotes `\"` around `telemetry_hook_bundle.js`.

---

Once you have applied either fix, reply to this message and I will immediately execute Task 6, verify with Node tests, and run `make autowf-test`.
